// Distinct CI test names, one row per test.
//
// A dimension table for ciTestResults, written by the same collector as
// ciJobOutcomes - see tooling/tenant-quota/pkg/cijoboutcomes. Test names are
// long and repeat on every run, so storing them once and joining on a short id
// keeps ciTestResults small and its queries fast.
//
// testId is the hex SHA-256 of the name, so it is stable across restarts and
// needs no coordination between writers: the same test always yields the same
// id. Names are never rewritten, so a name that disappears from the suite keeps
// its id and its history stays joinable.
//
// A name may appear more than once. The writer skips names already stored, but
// a queued row stays invisible to that check for several minutes, so two runs
// carrying a newly added test can both write it. Duplicates are identical by
// construction - the row is entirely determined by the id - so reading through
// distinct collapses them exactly, and the table is small enough for that to
// cost nothing:
//
//     ciTestResults
//     | join kind=inner (ciTestNames | distinct testId, name) on testId
.create-merge table ciTestNames (
    testId: string,
    name: string
)
with (
    docstring = "Distinct CI test names keyed by a stable hash, written by the opstool tenant-quota collector",
    folder = "CI"
)

.create-or-alter table ciTestNames ingestion json mapping "ciTestNamesMapping"
```
[
  {"column":"testId","path":"$['testId']","datatype":"string"},
  {"column":"name","path":"$['name']","datatype":"string"}
]
```
